Here's the status-filterable list. It uses two surfaces: a filter strip with status counts, and the eight-item list below it.

<a2ui-json>
[
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "status-filter",
      "catalogId": "https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/c-data-display.json"
    }
  },
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "updateComponents": {
      "surfaceId": "status-filter",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "segmented_control",
          "name": "status_filter",
          "selected_value": "all",
          "options": "[{\"label\": \"All (8)\", \"value\": \"all\"}, {\"label\": \"Active (3)\", \"value\": \"active\"}, {\"label\": \"Pending (2)\", \"value\": \"pending\"}, {\"label\": \"Blocked (1)\", \"value\": \"blocked\"}, {\"label\": \"Done (2)\", \"value\": \"done\"}]",
          "accessibility": {
            "label": "Filter by status",
            "description": "Shows only the items with the selected status"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "item-list",
      "catalogId": "https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/c-data-display.json"
    }
  },
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "updateComponents": {
      "surfaceId": "item-list",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "data_table_sortable",
          "headers": ["Title", "Status", "Detail"],
          "rows": [
            ["Onboarding flow redesign", "Active", "New welcome screens are in design review this week."],
            ["Billing API migration", "Active", "Moving invoice endpoints to the v2 gateway."],
            ["Search relevance tuning", "Active", "Testing a new ranking model on 10% of traffic."],
            ["Mobile push notifications", "Pending", "Waiting on copy approval from marketing."],
            ["Data retention policy", "Pending", "Legal review is scheduled for next Tuesday."],
            ["SSO for enterprise tenants", "Blocked", "Needs a SAML certificate from the identity team."],
            ["Dark mode support", "Done", "Shipped to all users in release 4.2."],
            ["Audit log export", "Done", "CSV and JSON export are now available in settings."]
          ],
          "accessibility": {
            "label": "Items",
            "description": "Eight items, each with a title, status, and one-line detail"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
]
</a2ui-json>

**About filtering:** this catalog has no data-binding or functions, so the status control can't automatically hide rows in the list. The selected filter value (`status_filter`) is available to the host application, which can use it to re-send the list with only the matching rows. In the meantime, you can sort by the **Status** column to group items by status.
